<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arab conquest of the Fezzan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">643–<a href="/years/670">670 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muslim-conquest-of-the-maghreb">Muslim conquest of the Maghreb</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Arab conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fezzan">Fezzan</a> was the series of Muslim Arab campaigns into the Fezzan region of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a> between 643 and 670 CE. Expeditions, including that associated with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uqba-ibn-nafi">Uqba ibn Nafi</a>, subdued the oases and imposed tribute. The conquest marked the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garamantian-empire">Garamantian Empire</a>'s independence.</p></div>
